Z||000000||Mark O'Hara||10-26-2000||10:28 PM||||How do I get around not having a 4t60e or 65e transaxle if I want to use the 97 PCM I got with my 3.4 DOHC? Does anybody know enough to take that section of the program out of the system? Or does anybody have a 4t65e for sale for a reasonable price? ($200 maybe?) I'm ready with the rest of the harness but from what I've seen here about erratic behavior and big resistors hanging out of the wiring harness,I need some advice and help. Thanks Mark||||reg||5
Z||000001||87GTZ34||10-28-2000||10:11 AM||||Mark,<P>  Without building electronics to 'fool' the computer, I'd hit up a GM shop to see if that engine was mated to a stick and if so, pay the whatever to have them reprogram the PCM.  IMHO this would be the cleanest possible solution.  If not hit up superchips, they may be able to help.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.superchips.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.superchips.com/</A> <BR><P>------------------<BR>87GTZ34||||reg||1
Z||000002||lowCG||10-28-2000||01:36 PM||||What I wanted to do was to get the software to modify the PCM's flash memory via laptop for $750,however I went with the fuel controller from Split Second($500) instead.The software would be a more correct way of doing things and would allow for the rev limiter to be moved as well.I was short on time in finishing my swap,but might be interested in the software yet, if I can get it to pay for itself or just not have to take the entire hit myself even.||||reg||1
